language-derived-from-the-record-7 = unlines (cons (quoted (cons "**5. Shared meaning is descent.** A participant's meaning of a word at a moment is the family of what followed the past occurrences its present context selects, each transported to now along the path identifying its context with the present one. Two participants i and j have different records, joined along shared events (one physical event received by both: the same light, the same sound) and along copying events (j's occurrence caused by i's production, or both by a common source); the records glued along these events form a joined record. j receives i's w as i means it exactly when j's transported family equals i's transported along the join: when the meaning computed over the joined part does not depend on what is not shared. Equal observations, equal outcomes: it is the descent theorem of the paper's §1 paragraph " (cons "A reversible whole with no observed law" (cons ", where a law on a whole J with step s gives a law on observations o exactly when o(j) = o(j′) implies o(s j) = o(s j′). That paragraph is about language too." nil)))) nil)
